 | ):\n 48 |     \"\"\"\n 49 |     Draw histogram of the input series using matplotlib.\n 50 | \n 51 |     Parameters\n 52 |     ----------\n 53 |     by : object, optional\n 54 |         If passed, then used to form histograms for separate groups.\n 55 |     ax : matplotlib axis object\n 56 |         If not passed, uses gca().\n 57 |     grid : bool, default True\n 58 |         Whether to show axis grid lines.\n 59 |     xlabelsize : int, default None\n 60 |         If specified changes the x-axis label size.\n 61 |     xrot : float, default None\n 62 |         Rotation of x axis labels.\n 63 |     ylabelsize : int, default None\n 64 |         If specified changes the y-axis label size.\n 65 |     yrot : float, default None\n 66 |         Rotation of y axis labels.\n 67 |     figsize : tuple, default None\n 68 |         Figure size in inches by default.\n 69 |     bins : int or sequence, default 10\n 70 |         Number of histogram bins to be used. If an integer is given, bins + 1\n 71 |         bin edges are calculated and returned. If bins is a sequence, gives\n 72 |         bin edges, including left edge of first bin and right edge of last\n 73 |         bin. In this case, bins is returned unmodified.\n 74 |     backend : str, default None\n 75 |         Backend to use instead of the backend specified in the option\n 76 |         ``plotting.backend``. For instance, 'matplotlib'. Alternatively, to\n 77 |         specify the ``plotting.backend`` for the whole session, set\n 78 |         ``pd.options.plotting.backend``.\n 79 | \n 80 |         .. versionadded:: 1.0.0\n 81 | \n 82 |     legend : bool, default False\n 83 |         Whether to show the legend.\n 84 | \n 85 |         .. versionadded:: 1.1.0\n 86 | \n 87 |     **kwargs\n 88 |         To be passed to the actual plotting function.\n 89 | \n 90 |     Returns\n 91 |     -------\n 92 |     matplotlib.AxesSubplot\n 93 |         A histogram plot.\n 94 | \n 95 |     See Also\n 96 |     --------\n 97 |     matplo