timator's fit method supports the given parameter.\n1512 | \n1513 |     Parameters\n1514 |     ----------\n1515 |     estimator : object\n1516 |         An estimator to inspect.\n1517 | \n1518 |     parameter : str\n1519 |         The searched parameter.\n1520 | \n1521 |     Returns\n1522 |     -------\n1523 |     is_parameter : bool\n1524 |         Whether the parameter was found to be a named parameter of the\n1525 |         estimator's fit method.\n1526 | \n1527 |     Examples\n1528 |     --------\n1529 |     >>> from sklearn.svm import SVC\n1530 |     >>> from sklearn.utils.validation import has_fit_parameter\n1531 |     >>> has_fit_parameter(SVC(), \"sample_weight\")\n1532 |     True\n1533 |     \"\"\"\n1534 |     return parameter in signature(estimator.fit).parameters\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/pipeline.py:Pipeline.set_params`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n214 | def set_params(self, **kwargs):\n215 |         \"\"\"Set the parameters of this estimator.\n216 | \n217 |         Valid parameter keys can be listed with ``get_params()``. Note that\n218 |         you can directly set the parameters of the estimators contained in\n219 |         `steps`.\n220 | \n221 |         Parameters\n222 |         ----------\n223 |         **kwargs : dict\n224 |             Parameters of this estimator or parameters of estimators contained\n225 |             in `steps`. Parameters of the steps may be set using its name and\n226 |             the parameter name separated by a '__'.\n227 | \n228 |         Returns\n229 |         -------\n230 |         self : object\n231 |             Pipeline class instance.\n232 |         \"\"\"\n233 |         self._set_params(\"steps\", **kwargs)\n234 |         return self\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/pipeline.py:FeatureUnion.set_params`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1496 | def set_params(self, **kwargs):\n1497 |         \"\"\"Set the parameters of this estimator.\n1