       left DataFrame. Must be None if either left or right are a Series.\n549 |     fill_method : {'ffill', None}, default None\n550 |         Interpolation method for data.\n551 |     suffixes : list-like, default is (\"_x\", \"_y\")\n552 |         A length-2 sequence where each element is optionally a string\n553 |         indicating the suffix to add to overlapping column names in\n554 |         `left` and `right` respectively. Pass a value of `None` instead\n555 |         of a string to indicate that the column name from `left` or\n556 |         `right` should be left as-is, with no suffix. At least one of the\n557 |         values must not be None.\n558 | \n559 |     how : {'left', 'right', 'outer', 'inner'}, default 'outer'\n560 |         * left: use only keys from left frame (SQL: left outer join)\n561 |         * right: use only keys from right frame (SQL: right outer join)\n562 |         * outer: use union of keys from both frames (SQL: full outer join)\n563 |         * inner: use intersection of keys from both frames (SQL: inner join).\n564 | \n565 |     Returns\n566 |     -------\n567 |     DataFrame\n568 |         The merged DataFrame output type will be the same as\n569 |         'left', if it is a subclass of DataFrame.\n570 | \n571 |     See Also\n572 |     --------\n573 |     merge : Merge with a database-style join.\n574 |     merge_asof : Merge on nearest keys.\n575 | \n576 |     Examples\n577 |     --------\n578 |     >>> from pandas import merge_ordered\n579 |     >>> df1 = pd.DataFrame(\n580 |     ...     {\n581 |     ...         \"key\": [\"a\", \"c\", \"e\", \"a\", \"c\", \"e\"],\n582 |     ...         \"lvalue\": [1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3],\n583 |     ...         \"group\": [\"a\", \"a\", \"a\", \"b\", \"b\", \"b\"],\n584 |     ...     }\n585 |     ... )\n586 |     >>> df1\n587 |       key  lvalue group\n588 |     0   a       1     a\n589 |     1   c       2     a\n590 |     2   e       3     a\n591 |     3   a       1     b\n592 |     4   c       2